#### Executive Summary
Transitioning autonomous agentic systems from prototype to production require=
s closing the 80% 'last mile' gap through an enterprise-grade operational dis=
cipline known as AgentOps. For systems architects, this shifts the paradigm f=
rom traditional MLOps to orchestrating stateful, non-deterministic execution =
paths, requiring strict evaluation-gated CI/CD pipelines, decoupled stateless=
 runtimes on Cloud Run or Vertex AI Agent Engine, and externalized state pers=
istence across AlloyDB and long-term memory stores. Production resilience hin=
ges on a three-tier defense-in-depth framework=E2=80=94anchoring System Instr=
uctions as a behavioral constitution, utilizing Agent Gateway and Model Armor=
 for real-time policy and injection filtering, and deploying runtime circuit =
breakers. At organizational scale, system modularity is achieved through a du=
al-protocol topology: leveraging the Model Context Protocol (MCP) for structu=
red, deterministic tool execution and the Agent2Agent (A2A) protocol with Age=
nt Cards for distributed, cross-team autonomous goal delegation.

#### Key Takeaways (Architect Track)
- Evaluation-Gated Promotion: Replace superficial unit tests with mandatory p=
re-merge and staging behavioral quality gates powered by golden datasets and =
LLM-as-a-judge, enforced via Terraform and GitOps with automated canary and b=
lue-green rollouts.
- Decoupled Compute and State Topology: Architect agent runtimes as horizonta=
lly scalable stateless microservices on Cloud Run or Agent Engine, offloading=
 long-running multi-turn execution to Pub/Sub queues and isolating session me=
mory into AlloyDB or Agent Memory Banks.
- Three-Layer Defense-in-Depth & Circuit Breakers: Mitigate prompt injection,=
 tool poisoning, and data leakage by enforcing System Instructions, routing t=
raffic through an Agent Gateway with Model Armor filters, and provisioning ru=
ntime circuit breakers to immediately sever compromised tool integrations.
- Complementary Interoperability (A2A vs. MCP): Partition agent capabilities =
cleanly=E2=80=94employ MCP for deterministic, structured tool execution ('do =
this specific task') and Linux Foundation A2A with JSON-based Agent Cards for=
 high-level, goal-oriented inter-agent delegation ('achieve this complex goal=
').
- Closed-Loop Observe-Act-Evolve Flywheel: Unify Cloud Trace, Logging, and Mo=
nitoring across multi-agent trajectories to automatically capture production =
failure modes and feed them back into regression evaluation suites within 48 =
hours.

